Presidential elections were held in [[El Salvador]] on 7 March 1999. The result was a victory for [[Francisco Flores (politician)|Francisco Flores]] of the [[Nationalist Republican Alliance]], who won in the first round with 51.96% of the vote.<ref name="Memoria Especial de Labores Elección 1999">{{cite web|url=https://www.tse.gob.sv/laip_tse/documentos/estadisticos/1999/consolidado_nacional_presid_1999.pdf|title=Memoria Especial de Labores Elección 1999|agency=Tribunal Supremo Electoral|date=2022-02-14|access-date=2022-03-10}}</ref>

